    <td align="left" width="100%" valign="top" colspan="2" bgcolor="EEEAE3" class="post-body" wrap height="115">Well, I thought I'd share a little of what I've been up to lately:<P>Besides the normal boring crap in life (work, work, work), I've replaced my EQ time quite wonderfully with my cello playing.  I've had 4 lessons so far & I can actually make some fairly recognizable sounds (albeit, sometimes not too pretty).  My two favorite "pieces" are "Ode to Joy" and "Can-Can dance".<P>But damn, I really miss you guys.  I find myself reading this message board several times a day, just enjoying the news of what's going on.  2 or 3 times a week, I stare at the computer for a bit, thinking, "I bet Silvermaine hasn't changed my password - I could just log in for a few minutes."  But somehow, I convince myself that practicing would be more fun.  <P>It's not more fun at all, but it's different; I feel like I'm leveling a new character in the pre-twink Norrath - it's slow.  However, I get great satisfaction out of "perfecting" a difficult sequence of notes that actually ends up sounding decent.<P>Other than work & cello practice, my life's been pretty boring...my wife & I were up in Chatanooga (sp?) for a few days - camping, hiking, and of course, we had to "See Rock City".  We're also in the middle of renovating our master bathroom.  <P>Oh yeah...I've started training for a 50 mile run in December.  That's something "Tobuk/Die t-sip" & I are doing together.<P>Anyway...I miss you guys.<P>As my wife always tells me, "Play nice with the other geeks!"</td>
