    <td align="left" width="100%" valign="top" colspan="2" bgcolor="EEEAE3" class="post-body" wrap height="115">Lyrik - <BR>1.  Yes our old boss (frank) is playing.  I don't think you know any of the other people - they're all new (within the past 2 years).<P>2.  Die & I live 45 miles apart.  However, every Saturday morning, we meet in the middle (Memorial Park) & run from there.  It's much easier to do a 2 hour run with a friend - otherwise, you just get bored to tears.<P>3.  Chatanooga was beautiful.  I guess I was fortunate enough to miss all the ticks.  We didn't get to white water raft, even though I really wanted to (the outfitters were only open on the weekends - before summer, this seems to be common).  In any case, I don't think I would be up for Class V rapids - Class IV would be enough to make me happy.<P>However, we went & saw a couple of caves & had a blast.  We'll probably return sometime in the next year for a 6 hour caving trip where you go through crawl-ways, get muddy, and see some parts of the caves that are very pretty.</td>
  </tr>
